{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nT11's POST-ROLLBACK SCHEMA STATE paragraph is a stock-finding generator: 8 of 21 sampled findings were near-identical \"plan does not assert post-rollback state\" advisories that are tautologies against an append-only store (median priority ~0.1), drowning its rare real catches (e.g. the 114f fold-in overwrite data-loss bug). The operator approved a constraint and rejected a per-plan cap; the constraint must be portable across stacks (no store technology named).\n\n## Approach\nReplace the post-rollback paragraph in src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_T11.md with a four-condition applicability rule: raise post-rollback-state findings ONLY when the plan (a) changes how existing persisted records are interpreted, (b) rewrites or migrates records in place, (c) removes or narrows a read path, or (d) performs a one-way transformation with no back-out. Add the explicit anti-false-positive line: purely additive, backward-compatible persistence changes that existing readers ignore (new record/event types, optional fields, new tables or columns with defaults) do not qualify — residual data after rollback is the norm in append-only and backward-compatible systems, not a risk. No store technology is named in the applicability rule itself, so it applies equally to SQL migrations, event stores, document databases, and config formats. Posture stays advisory. Alternative rejected: a one-finding-per-plan cap — operator rejected it; the applicability rule removes the tautology class at the source instead.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_T11.md, tests/unit/test_plan_review_t11_rubric.py (new, beside the other plan-review rubric contract tests in tests/unit/), docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md (regenerated).\n\n## Testing\nRubric text assertions in tests/unit/test_plan_review_t11_rubric.py: the four conditions and the anti-FP line are present; the old unconditional post-rollback wording is gone; the applicability rule names no store technology (the illustrative anti-FP examples are exempt from that assertion).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The rubric raises post-rollback findings only under the four named conditions (checked: `pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_t11_rubric.py` asserting the conditions and absence of the old wording).\n- [ ] The anti-FP line for additive backward-compatible changes is present (checked: same test file).\n- [ ] The criteria guide is regenerated (checked: committed regen output)."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785388175557146001,"uuid":"a1e2d6c9-850b-4b63-8f4f-73cb74180c2c"}